name issue_62_neteq_v2_high_jitter
describe high_jitter with NetEq's target delay (neteq v2, issue #62): buffer as libwebrtc, conceal as little
duration 30s
neteq v2
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=30ms jitter=40ms reorder=on queue=300ms
# libwebrtc M157 on high_jitter (compare-webrtc, seeds 1-10): concealed 0.07-0.27 %,
# jitter buffer delay p95 100-130 ms. neteq v1: concealed 1.17-1.64 %, p95 72-88 ms.
expect audio.interruptions == 0
expect audio.concealed_pct < 0.5
expect audio.jb_delay_p95_ms >= 95
# PR for #375 (Opus size model calibrated to libopus; the start probe moves; program.md 0.2, needs-human): was <= 140. Ours 150 on seed 1;
# libwebrtc 100 on seed 1, worst of seeds 1-10 150 (mean 122; ours 136, in band), on #324's compare-webrtc.
# PR for #457 (libopus 55513e81 replaces the Opus size model; program.md 0.2, needs-human): was <= 150. Ours 170 on seed 1
# (seeds 1-10 100-170, mean 133); libwebrtc seeds 1-10 100-170 (mean 130) on main's compare-webrtc. Capped at libwebrtc's worst seed.
# PR for #476 (our side decodes with libopus as libwebrtc does; harness change, needs-human): was <= 170. Ours 180 on
# seed 1 (seeds 1-10 100-180, mean 132, was 133); libwebrtc seeds 1-10 100-180 (mean 129) on main's compare-webrtc
# (9e436cb). Capped at libwebrtc's worst seed, as for #457.
expect audio.jb_delay_p95_ms <= 180
